cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KLM or klm-conformance, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "KLM — Knowledge Layers Model: specification and klm-conformance toolchain"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/omasim/KLM"
url: "https://github.com/omasim/KLM"
abstract: "KLM is a vendor-neutral reference model for attestable knowledge in language-model systems: a layered attestation record with explicit epistemic status on every signal, a deterministic mechanical floor, separate declared and grounded confidence, and staged conformance levels. klm-conformance is the stdlib-only reference verifier (validators, Ed25519 envelopes, hash-chained logs, disclosure views)."
